            content: `### Unit Objectives
Listen and take notes from a story; read and identify main ideas; write a paragraph on health and fitness lessons; use conditional sentences; guess meanings from context; discuss health and fitness; reflect and self-assess.

### 2.1 Listening: Zinedine Zidane
- **Activity 2.1.1: Pre-Listening Key Vocabulary Distinctions**:
  - **Career**: An occupation or series of jobs/roles that a person undertakes over a significant period of their life, with opportunities for progress (e.g., *"Zidane had an extraordinary football **career**"*).
  - **Profession**: A paid occupation, especially one that involves **prolonged training and a formal qualification** (e.g., medicine, teaching, engineering, law).
  - **Professional**: (1) *Adjective*: Relating to or belonging to a profession, or engaging in a sport/activity as a paid job rather than as a pastime (*amateur*); (2) *Noun*: A person engaged or qualified in a profession or paid sport.
  - **Word Forms**: *jog* (base verb / noun: a slow regular run for fitness) $\\rightarrow$ *jogged* (past simple/participle) $\\rightarrow$ *jogging* (gerund/present participle).
- **Activity 2.1.2: Zinedine Zidane Biographical Fact Sheet (While-Listening Table)**:
  - **Full Name**: Zinedine Yazid Zidane (nicknamed *"Zizou"*).
  - **Date & Place of Birth**: June 23, 1972, in La Castellane, **Marseille, France** (of Algerian Kabyle descent).
  - **Known For**: Being one of the greatest football players and playmakers in history, renowned for elegance, ball control, vision, and later coaching Real Madrid to three consecutive UEFA Champions League titles.
  - **Playing Position**: Attacking Midfielder (Playmaker / #10).
  - **Clubs Played For**: Cannes, Bordeaux, **Juventus** (Italy), and **Real Madrid** (Spain).
  - **Real Madrid Transfer Fee**: A then-world-record fee of **77.5 million euros** (approx. $150 billion Italian lire) in 2001.
  - **Major Trophies & Games Won**: **1998 FIFA World Cup** (scored two headers in the 3–0 final win against Brazil) and **UEFA Euro 2000** with France; UEFA Champions League (2002, scoring a famous left-foot volley in the final) with Real Madrid; named **FIFA World Player of the Year three times** (1998, 2000, 2003) and won the **1998 Ballon d'Or**.
  - **Special Points**: Won the Golden Ball as best player of the 2006 World Cup, though infamously sent off in his final career match (the 2006 World Cup Final) for headbutting Marco Materazzi; also served as UN Goodwill Ambassador against poverty.

### 2.2 Grammar Focus: Conditionals (Types I, II, and III)
Conditional sentences consist of two clauses: the **Condition Clause (*If*-clause / Subordinate Clause)** and the **Result Clause (Main Clause)**. *(Punctuation Rule: When the If-clause comes first, separate the two clauses with a **comma**; when the main clause comes first, **no comma** is used).*

| Conditional Type | Meaning & Time Reference | *If*-Clause (Condition) | Main Clause (Result) | Example (Derartu Tulu / Zidane / Fitness) |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Zero Conditional** | Scientific facts, general truths | **If + Simple Present** ($V_1/V_s$) | **Simple Present** ($V_1/V_s$) | *If you **exercise** regularly, your heart **becomes** stronger.* |
| **Type I (Real / Probable)** | Real or very likely future possibility | **If + Simple Present** ($V_1/V_s$) | **will / can / may / should + Base Verb ($V_1$)** | *If you **train** hard every day, you **will win** the race.* |
| **Type II (Unreal / Hypothetical Present or Future)** | Imaginary, improbable, or contrary-to-fact situation in the **present or future** | **If + Simple Past** ($V_2$; use **were** for all persons!) | **would / could / might + Base Verb ($V_1$)** | *What **would** you **do** if you **were** the mother?* / *If I **were** as talented as Derartu Tulu, I **would compete** in the Olympics.* |
| **Type III (Unreal / Impossible Past)** | Imaginary or contrary-to-fact situation in the **past** (regret/criticism; cannot be changed now) | **If + Past Perfect** (**had + $V_3$**) | **would / could / might + have + Past Participle ($V_3$)** | *If Zidane **had not lost** his temper in 2006, France **might have won** the World Cup.* |`
